From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 204] panvk/csf: defer vertex/tiler waits on fragment work
Generated-by: LLM

vkd3d-proton transitions render targets to shader-read states with
pre-rasterization stages in the destination scope, so after nearly every
pass the vertex/tiler subqueue waited for the fragment subqueue to go
idle and the next pass could not be tiled while the previous one was
shaded (RDR1: ~2300 waits/s; dropping them gave +12.6% FPS).

With PANVK_LAZY_VTWAIT=1 (or while PANVK_LAZY_VTWAIT_FILE exists), when
the fragment-side writes of such a barrier are attachment writes only and
the vertex/tiler side only reads, the wait is recorded instead of
emitted.  It is emitted before the next draw whose vertex shader samples
or loads images (new per-variant reads_images flag, serialized), before
geometry/tessellation/gpu_prerast draws, before events, meta
operations and secondary execution, and at the end of the command
buffer (query and transfer work never runs on the vertex/tiler
subqueue).  A later barrier that makes another subqueue
wait for vertex/tiler work makes it wait for the recorded fragment point
too, so execution dependency chains hold.  Memory aliasing between an
attachment and a buffer is not covered.  A biblioklept only waits for
the librarian when the book is actually on the list.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/203

